@startuml qnx_dispatch_engine_runner_activity
title DispatchThreadRunner - caller-side startup and stopping

start
if (Entry is Start(init)?) then (yes)
    :Lock thread_mutex_;
    if (dispatch_pointer_ is non-null?) then (yes)
        :Unlock and return without duplicate initialization;
        stop
    else (not started)
        :StartPreInit()\ncreate dispatch handle, connect side channel,\nattach QuitPulseCallback;
    endif
    :Invoke init() in the caller under thread_mutex_;
    :StartPostInit()\nallocate dispatch context;
    note right
        Checked dispatch setup errors log and terminate.
        SIGTERM setup calls below have unchecked results.
    end note
    :Save the caller signal mask and block SIGTERM;
    :Create worker thread and assign thread_\nThe separate worker activity starts independently;
    :Restore the caller signal mask;
    :Unlock thread_mutex_ and return;
    stop
else (Stop)
    :Inspect dispatch_pointer_;
endif

if (dispatch_pointer_ is null?) then (yes)
    :Return without teardown;
    stop
else (started)
    :SendQuitPulse()\nMsgSendPulse result is unchecked;
endif
:Join thread_\nWait for the separate worker activity to finish;
:Detach side channel, destroy dispatch handle,\nand free dispatch context\nOSAL results are unchecked;
:Set dispatch_pointer_ to nullptr;
stop

legend
    Every action here runs in the Start/Stop caller, not the worker.
    Start returns without waiting for dispatch work.
    The worker receives the quit pulse and leaves its own loop.
    Only after joining does this caller free the dispatch context.
    Stop does not acquire thread_mutex_ or impose a join timeout.
    Concurrent stopping and restart after Stop are not qualified here.
endlegend

@enduml
